 ### CLI Usage

-Mounting / unlocking a vault:
+The `plasma-vault` command lists, unlocks and locks vaults. A vault can be given by its name, its mount point or its encrypted folder.

 ```sh
-qdbus org.kde.kded6 /modules/plasmavault org.kde.plasmavault.openVault "<absolute path of encrypted backing folder>"
+plasma-vault list
+plasma-vault open <vault>
+plasma-vault close <vault>
+plasma-vault close --all
 ```

-Unmounting / re-locking a vault:
-
-```sh
-qdbus org.kde.kded6 /modules/plasmavault org.kde.plasmavault.closeVault "<absolute path of encrypted backing folder>"
-```
-
-Note: depending on your distro, `qdbus` may be named `qdbus6` or `qdbus-qt6`.
+Unlocking asks for the password in the usual Plasma Vault dialog, so the password is never passed on the command line. `close --force` closes the applications that are using the vault before locking it.

 ### Migrating old mountpoints

